<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Mohawk Nation</h1><p class="st-meta">1450 CE – present (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The People of the Flint, Keepers of the Eastern Door of the Iroquois Confederacy, key partners of the Dutch and British and today spread across New York, Quebec and Ontario.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Mohawk lived in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohawk-river">Mohawk River</a> valley of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, the easternmost of the five <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/iroquois-confederacy">Haudenosaunee</a> nations. Haudenosaunee tradition holds that they were the first nation to accept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-peacemaker">the Peacemaker's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-law-of-peace">Great Law of Peace</a>, around the mid-15th century, and so hold an elder place in the Iroquois <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/confederate-states-of-america">Confederacy</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nine Mohawk chiefs sat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-council-qing">Grand Council</a>. Trade with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-netherland">New Netherland</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-orange">Fort Orange</a> from the 1610s gave the Mohawk firearms and made them leading players in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">fur trade</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beaver-wars">Beaver Wars</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> missions drew Catholic converts north, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kateri-tekakwitha">Kateri Tekakwitha</a>, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kahnawake">Kahnawake</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montreal">Montreal</a>. In the 18th century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hendrick-theyanoguin">Hendrick Theyanoguin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molly-brant">Molly Brant</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-brant">Joseph Brant</a> built close ties with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> and the Indian superintendent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-johnson">William Johnson</a>.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>After fighting for <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> in the Revolution, most Mohawk left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-river-ontario">Grand River</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyendinaga-mohawk-territory">Tyendinaga</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>. Mohawk communities today include <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akwesasne">Akwesasne</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kahnawake">Kahnawake</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanesatake">Kanesatake</a>, scene of the 1990 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oka-crisis">Oka crisis</a>, along with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/iroquois-confederacy">Six Nations</a> and Tyendinaga in Ontario.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/mohawk-nation.jpg" alt="Mohawk Nation" width="320" height="384"><figcaption>Image: Gilbert Stuart · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joseph_Brant_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1450 CE – present (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hendrick Theyanoguin, Joseph Brant</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Haudenosaunee traditional religion, Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mohawk</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a>, <a href="/countries/canada">Canada</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kanienkehaka, Mohawk</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1738&amp;focus=mohawk-nation" aria-label="Mohawk Nation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2279 779 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Mohawk Nation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3160 908h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2599 1035h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M2599 1035h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day United States. <a href="/atlas?year=1738&amp;focus=mohawk-nation">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

